From 17601bcd30c8cb15576d04d92f5b1d6af795cba1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 05:01:52 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 86/86] go.mod: golang.org/x/net v0.57.0, with x/crypto, x/text
 and x/sys, as the 1.14 line

x/net v0.50.0 calls a nil parser for HTTP/2 frames of types 0x0a to 0x0f: one such frame
from a server the HTTP/2 client talks to (DNS over HTTPS, the gRPC, HTTP and xhttp
transports, the request after a failed REALITY verification) ends the process, in a
goroutine of the library that sing-box cannot guard. The same version loops forever on a
SETTINGS_MAX_FRAME_SIZE of zero. Both are fixed upstream by v0.53.0.

The versions are those sing-box 1.14.2 is built and tested with; the go directive becomes
1.25.0, which they require.
---
 go.mod | 18 +++++++++---------
 go.sum | 32 ++++++++++++++++----------------
 2 files changed, 25 insertions(+), 25 deletions(-)

